# Output folder

Every file this plugin creates goes in `adrenaline/ux-writing/` at the project root.

If `.cursor/adrenaline.json` exists and `outputDirs["plugin-ux-writing"]` holds a path, use that path. The path is relative to the project root, with no `..` and not absolute. If it is not valid, use `adrenaline/ux-writing/` and say so.

If `adrenaline/ux-writing/` does not exist yet and `ux-writing/` at the project root already has this plugin's `ORIGIN.json` or `STATUS.md`, keep writing there and say so.

Create the folder if it does not exist. Do not write anywhere else.

A numbered file about one named project, app, service, or domain goes in `<subject>/`. A numbered file about the whole product stays at this folder's root. `<NNN>` is the next free number in the whole output folder. The `archivo` cell is `<subject>/<file>` when there is a subject. This is `doc/arch/adr-008-asunto-subcarpeta.md`.


Write the artifact in the language of the request. If the request names a language, use that one. Otherwise use the language the request is written in. Keep names the person already used. The type in the file name stays the English piece id. `STATUS.md` columns stay `N`, `archivo`, `estado`, `sustituye`, `notas`.

Keep `ORIGIN.json` in that folder, beside `STATUS.md`. The fields are `suite` `ADRenaline-Suite`, `plugin` `plugin-ux-writing`, `repository` `https://github.com/ADRenaline-Suite/plugin-ux-writing`, and `convention` `adr-001`. It is not an `<NNN>` file and it has no row in `STATUS.md`. Write it when the folder is created, and again only if it is missing or a field differs. The marker names the folder. It does not say that each file inside is unchanged.
